  "title": "Alawieh2025: Motor-imagery BCI dataset with transcutaneous spinal stimulation",
  "description": "A longitudinal EEG dataset of two-class (left vs. right hand) motor-imagery brain-computer interface (BCI) training combined with transcutaneous electrical spinal cord stimulation. It includes 27 participants (25 able-bodied and 2 with spinal cord injury) recorded with a 32-channel EEG montage plus EOG at 512 Hz. The dataset supports research on how spinal stimulation affects sensorimotor activation and BCI skill learning.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with an ANT Neuro eego amplifier using Ag/AgCl electrodes (32 EEG and 3 EOG channels, 512 Hz, CPz reference, AFz ground). Participants performed cue-based, offline left-hand and right-hand kinesthetic motor imagery in 4 s trials, with transcutaneous spinal stimulation.",
